          "spec": "3D: a double cone and a cutting plane; a tilt slider sweeps circle → ellipse → parabola → hyperbola. Angle rule: compare the plane's tilt with the cone's side: less steep gives an ellipse, equal a parabola, steeper a hyperbola. Flatten: the cut curve drawn in 2D beside its equation. History note: Apollonius named them around 200 BC.",
